# ============================================================
#  Minor chains: short cause-and-effect stories.
#    forbidden  — the Restricted Section key (from umbral_forbidden_notes)
#    curse      — curing the Umbral Curse
#    debt       — Grisk the moneylender (see state in_debt)
#    familiar   — Ember the fox-spirit
#    ghost      — the haunted dormitory
# ============================================================

# ---------------- The Restricted Section ----------------

@event forbidden_section_1
title: The Silver Key
trigger: queued
art: key
tags: mystery
chain: forbidden
scene: A heavy iron door at the end of a library aisle, a silver key turning in its lock, a candle held low.
text: Midnight. The silver key fits the Restricted Section door perfectly. Beyond it, shelves of black-bound books breathe softly in the dark. Somewhere, a prefect's footsteps.
> left: Turn back
  mood -1
  flag forbidden_abandoned
  say: You lock the door again and hang the key on a nail in your wardrobe. Some nights you hear it rattling.
> right: Slip inside
  check guile 14:
    lore +4
    queue forbidden_section_2 in 2
    say: You spend two hours reading by candle-stub. You leave with a head full of things no first-year should know.
  else:
    gain detention
    gain watched
    rel bram -6
    say: Bram Hollis is waiting by the door when you come out. He is smiling. It's the worst smile you've ever seen.

@event forbidden_section_2
title: The Codex of Hollow Names
trigger: queued
art: book
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: forbidden
scene: A book bound in something that is not leather, open on a reading stand, its letters slowly rearranging themselves.
text: On your third visit, a book finds you. It falls from a high shelf and lands open at your feet: the Codex of Hollow Names. The first page is a list of names. The last one is still being written. It's yours.
> left: Put it back
  mood -2
  say: You shelve it. When you look back, it has fallen again, open at the same page.
> right: Read it
  lore +3
  arcana +3
  hollow +1
  queue forbidden_section_3 in 2
  chance 45:
    gain umbral_curse
    say: You read until dawn. You learn about the thing under the lake. When you finally close the book, your fingertips are grey.
  else:
    say: You read until dawn and close the book with shaking hands. Some things you can't unread.

@event forbidden_section_3
title: Caught
trigger: queued
actor: isolde
art: lock
tags: mystery
chain: forbidden
scene: A tall silhouette in the doorway of the Restricted Section, holding a lantern that casts long shadows over a startled student.
text: A lantern blazes in the doorway. Not a prefect this time: the headmistress herself. She looks at the book in your hands, then at you, for a very long time. "Most students who find that book," she says, "don't put it down."
> left: Apologise and accept punishment
  meet isolde
  grades -6
  gain detention
  rel isolde +3
  unflag forbidden_key
  say: She takes the key. "Detention. And come to my tower on Thursdays. If you're going to learn dangerous things, you'll learn them properly."
> right: Ask her what it means
  meet isolde
  rel isolde +6
  lore +3
  hollow +1
  unflag forbidden_key
  say: A long pause. "It means something is waking, and it is looking for help. Make sure it doesn't find yours." She takes the key and leaves you the candle.

# ---------------- The Umbral Curse ----------------

@event curse_cure_1
title: A Cold That Won't Leave
when: has(umbral_curse)
weight: 30
art: skull
tags: crisis mystery
chain: curse
scene: A student wrapped in three blankets beside a roaring fire, breath still fogging the air, fingertips grey.
text: The cold under your skin is getting worse. Sister Amaranth's tonics do nothing. She looks troubled. "This isn't an illness. It's a hunger." She lowers her voice. "Old Maud might know something. Don't tell anyone I said so."
> left: Endure it
  mood -3
  arcana +1
  say: You pile on blankets and keep going. The cold whispers sometimes. You pretend not to hear.
> right: Go to Old Maud
  meet maud
  rel maud +3
  queue curse_cure_2 in 1
  say: Maud takes one look at your fingertips and puts the kettle on. "Moonpetal," she says. "Grows in the Whisperwood. Only blooms at midnight. You'll fetch it yourself — the cure has to come from the cursed."

@event curse_cure_2
title: Moonpetal
trigger: queued
art: flower
tags: nature danger
chain: curse
scene: A dark forest at midnight, a single silver flower glowing in a clearing, eyes watching from between the trees.
text: The Whisperwood at midnight. Things move between the trees. In a clearing, a single silver flower is opening, and between you and it stands a stag made of shadow.
> left: Sneak around it
  check guile 16:
    lose umbral_curse
    rel maud +8
    say: You creep through the bracken and pluck the moonpetal. Maud's brew tastes like moonlight and burnt sugar. The cold is gone.
  else:
    health -10
    queue curse_cure_2 in 2
    say: The stag sees you. You run. No moonpetal tonight. Maud says the next bloom is in two months.
> right: Face the stag
  check vigor 18:
    lose umbral_curse
    vigor +2
    rel maud +8
    say: You stand your ground. The stag lowers its head — and steps aside. Maud's brew drives the cold out of your bones.
  else:
    health -12
    queue curse_cure_2 in 2
    say: The stag charges. You wake up in the bracken at dawn. Maud bandages you. "Again in two months," she says.

# ---------------- Grisk the Moneylender ----------------

@event grisk_offer
title: A Helpful Goblin
when: gold < 15 and turn >= 3 and not has(in_debt) and not flag(grisk_done)
weight: 30
art: pouch
tags: money danger
chain: debt
scene: A small goblin in a velvet waistcoat and pince-nez, sitting on a crate in an alley, a ledger in one hand and a quill behind his ear.
text: A goblin in a velvet waistcoat falls into step beside you. "Grisk," he says, "friend to the temporarily embarrassed. Sixty crowns, today. Twelve a month for six months. Very reasonable."
> left: No thank you
  mood -1
  say: "My door is always open," Grisk says. You suspect it is actually always locked.
> right: Take the loan
  gold +60
  gain in_debt
  debt_paid = 0
  debt_missed = 0
  flag grisk_done
  say: He counts out sixty crowns, writes your name in the ledger and smiles with a great many teeth.

@event grisk_favour
title: Grisk's Proposition
when: has(in_debt)
weight: 14
art: chain
tags: money mystery
chain: debt
scene: The goblin moneylender leaning close in a library alcove, pushing a slip of paper across a table.
text: Grisk finds you in the library. "I could cancel your debt," he murmurs. "A small favour. There's a book in the archive — the Founders' Ledger. A client wants a page. Just one page."
> left: Refuse
  say: "Pity." He makes a note in his ledger. It looks expensive.
> right: Do the favour
  check guile 18:
    lose in_debt
    flag grisk_favour
    hollow +1
    say: You razor a page from the oldest ledger in the archive. Grisk tears up your debt. You notice the page had a black star on it.
  else:
    gain detention
    grades -5
    say: The archivist catches you with a razor in your hand. Detention. Grisk is nowhere to be found, and the debt stands.

@event grisk_smuggling
title: One More Job
when: flag(grisk_favour) and not has(in_debt)
weight: 10
art: pouch
tags: money danger
chain: debt
scene: A crate of clinking bottles hidden under a tarp on a dark boathouse dock, a small goblin silhouetted against the lake.
text: Grisk again. "You were so good last time. A crate needs moving across the lake tonight. Don't open it. Forty crowns."
> left: You're done with him
  unflag grisk_favour
  mood +3
  say: "Everyone's done with me eventually," Grisk says, without rancour. You never see him again.
> right: Move the crate
  check guile 16:
    gold +40
    say: The crate clinks. It is also, faintly, singing. You deliver it without looking inside. Forty crowns.
  else:
    gold +10
    gain detention
    rel bram -8
    say: Bram stops you on the dock. The crate is full of contraband charm-wine. You lose the crate, keep ten crowns and gain a detention.

# ---------------- Ember the Fox-Spirit ----------------

@event fox_injured
title: Smoke in the Woods
when: turn >= 4 and not flag(fox_met)
weight: 6 + flag(familiar_affinity) * 14
art: fox
tags: nature
chain: familiar
scene: A small red fox lying in the snow at the forest edge, its tail smouldering like a dying campfire, one paw caught in a rusted snare.
text: At the edge of the forest, a thin plume of smoke. A small fox is caught in a rusted snare, its tail smouldering like an ember. It snarls at you, then whimpers.
> left: Leave it — it's wild
  mood -3
  say: You walk away. That night you dream of smoke.
> right: Free it and bandage the paw
  flag fox_met
  health -3
  gold -5
  queue fox_returns in 2
  say: It bites you, of course. But it lets you wrap the paw. Then it limps into the trees, glancing back once with eyes like embers.

@event fox_returns
title: A Visitor at the Window
trigger: queued
art: fox
tags: nature
chain: familiar
scene: A fox with a softly glowing tail sitting on a stone windowsill at dawn, a ruby glinting at its feet.
text: Two months later, a fox with a glowing tail is sitting on your windowsill. Its paw has healed. At its feet: a small, dusty ruby.
> left: Shoo it away
  gold +15
  say: It leaves the ruby and vanishes. You sell the ruby. Somehow you feel you've failed a test.
> right: Open the window
  gold +15
  mood +4
  queue fox_bond in 1
  say: It hops in, inspects your room thoroughly and falls asleep on your pillow. Your pillow is now slightly scorched. You don't mind.

@event fox_bond
title: Ember
trigger: queued
art: fox
tags: nature magic
chain: familiar
scene: A student and a small fire-tailed fox nose to nose, a soft golden light connecting them.
text: The fox has decided. It follows you to class, sleeps on your feet and growls at Bram. Students aren't allowed unregistered familiars. Registering one costs twenty crowns.
> left: Hide her (Guile)
  check guile 12:
    gain familiar_fox
    say: You name her Ember. Nobody notices a fox that doesn't want to be noticed.
  else:
    gain familiar_fox
    gold -20
    say: A professor spots her at once. You pay the fee — and Ember is yours, officially.
> right: Register her properly
  gold -20
  gain familiar_fox
  rel isolde +2
  say: The registrar stamps a form. "Name?" "Ember," you say. The fox looks smug.

@event fox_helps
title: Ember Finds Something
when: has(familiar_fox)
weight: 10
repeat: 8
art: fox
tags: nature
chain: familiar
scene: A fox nosing through dry leaves under a hedge and emerging with a purse in its jaws.
text: Ember drags you, by the sleeve, through three corridors and a hedge. She's found something. She's very proud of it.
> left: Let her keep it
  mood +4
  say: It's a sock. Ember is thrilled. You are thrilled for her.
> right: See what it is
  chance 50:
    gold +20
    say: A lost purse. You return it to its owner, who insists you keep the reward.
  else:
    lore +2
    say: A lost page from a professor's lecture notes. Enlightening.

# ---------------- The Haunted Dormitory ----------------

@event ghost_socks
title: Rearranged Socks
when: turn >= 3 and not flag(ghost_met)
weight: 8
art: ghost
tags: mystery
chain: ghost
scene: A dormitory drawer open in candlelight, socks arranged in a careful spiral, a faint shimmer in the air above them.
text: Every morning, your socks have been rearranged. By colour. Then alphabetically by colour. Last night they spelled out "HELP".
> left: Ignore it
  gain haunted
  say: You buy new socks. The next morning they're arranged by mood.
> right: Stay up and watch
  flag ghost_met
  gain haunted
  queue ghost_reveal now
  say: At three in the morning, the drawer slides open by itself.

@event ghost_reveal
title: Prudence
trigger: queued
art: ghost
tags: mystery
chain: ghost
scene: A translucent girl in old-fashioned school robes, hovering by a window, holding a faded letter.
text: A girl in old-fashioned robes, translucent and very polite. "Prudence Ashworth, class of 1793. Terribly sorry about the socks. I never finished my letter. Could you deliver it? The village. The bakery. Please."
> left: Exorcise her
  lose haunted
  arcana +1
  mood -2
  say: You speak the banishing rite. She fades with a small, hurt look. Your socks stay put after that. You feel a bit rotten.
> right: Promise to deliver it
  rel maud +2
  queue ghost_letter in 1
  say: She claps her translucent hands. "Oh, thank you! It's only taken two hundred years."

@event ghost_letter
title: A Letter Two Hundred Years Late
trigger: queued
art: letter
tags: mystery social
scene: A cosy village bakery, an old baker reading a yellowed letter with tears on her cheeks, a ghostly figure smiling in the doorway.
text: The bakery has been in the same family for two hundred years. The old baker reads Prudence's letter at the counter. "My great-great-great-grandmother waited for this," she says. "She never stopped."
> left: Stay and listen to the story
  lose haunted
  mood +10
  lore +2
  say: Prudence was in love with the baker's daughter. When you return, the ghost is waiting, glowing like a sunrise. Then she's gone, at peace.
> right: Leave quietly
  lose haunted
  mood +6
  renown +2
  say: The baker presses a free loaf into your hands. That night, your socks are arranged into a heart. Then never again.
